    <briefdescription>
<para>Scoped thread-local entropy override for the current request. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Use this when a caller already has exact entropy inputs for the current thread and wants <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1rag_1_1_t_a_r_g_retrieval_1a789a70b877638fb64029bec37b58c6db" kindref="member">gate()</ref></computeroutput> to reuse them without mutating the global <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1rag_1_1_t_a_r_g_retrieval_1a7dc66eac78ed4aea10a29125b4cd66bc" kindref="member">FullEntropyFn</ref></computeroutput> bridge for other requests. The scoped override takes precedence over the global callback while the guard is alive and is automatically removed at scope exit. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
